{:adr-id "2613300000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-2399 (manufacture of other non-metallic mineral products n.e.c.) plant-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR fresh-scaffold protocol per cloud-itonami-isic-2391 (refractory products, closest architectural sibling)"]

 :context
 "Live kotoba-lang/industry registry re-verified fresh before work began: :name
  'Manufacture of other non-metallic mineral products n.e.c.' confirmed for
  {:id \"2399\"} (:maturity :spec, stale placeholder :repo/:business-id
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2399 predating the current cloud-itonami-isic-<id>
  naming convention). No prior cloud-itonami-isic-2399 repo existed (gh api
  404 before this work began). ISIC 2399 is a residual ('not elsewhere
  classified') category with no dedicated product vocabulary of its own
  (mineral wool/insulation, abrasive products, asbestos products, mica
  products, etc.) -- this build picks ONE concrete illustrative product line
  (mineral wool / rock wool insulation manufacturing) rather than modeling the
  category abstractly. Built from cloud-itonami-isic-2391 (refractory
  products) as the module-structure template -- closest architectural
  sibling: same plant fixed-processing-line shape with a real physical safety
  dimension, same four-op shape, same two-entity (equipment + batch)
  verified/registered gate structure. Retargeted from refractory
  fire-brick/kiln-lining manufacturing to mineral-wool-insulation
  manufacturing (melting/fiberizing/binder-application/curing-oven-cure/
  cutting lines), distinct from both 2391 (refractories) and 2393 (porcelain
  and ceramic products)."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct forming/curing-line equipment control (cupola melter, fiberizing
   spinner, binder applicator, curing oven, cutting line -- plant
   supervisor's exclusive authority)"
  "direct forming/curing-line actuation (:actuate-forming-curing-line? true
   is a permanent, unconditional governor block)"
  "plant-safety decisions (respirable mineral-fibre exposure judgment,
   binder off-gassing/VOC exposure judgment remain human)"
  "real freight dispatch (this actor only drafts a shipment-coordination
   record, never dispatches a carrier)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-2399 with Advisor/Governor/Phase/Registry/Store/
  Operation/Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-2391 module-for-module, adapted
  from refractory-products to mineral-wool-insulation manufacturing --
  mineralwoolmfg.* namespace, Mineral Wool Plant Operations Governor):
  - Governor: eleven concrete HARD checks elaborating four HARD invariants
    (propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
    allowlist / no direct forming-curing-line control, permanent
    forming-curing-line-actuate block) plus a confidence/high-stakes
    escalation gate (SOFT, human may approve)
  - Registry: pure functions -- equipment/batch verified+registered gates,
    shipment-weight-exceeded recompute, product-type-valid? (8-member closed
    set: batt/roll/loose-fill/rigid-board/pipe-section/duct-wrap insulation,
    acoustic-panel, fire-stop-wrap), thermal-conductivity-valid?
    (0.020-0.060 W/(m*K)), density-valid? (8-250 kg/m^3) -- replacing 2391's
    thermal-shock-cycles/cold-crushing-strength-mpa pair
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (SSoT + append-only audit ledger,
    sample batches/equipment seeded for offline tests/demo)
  - Advisor: MineralWoolAdvisor -- deterministic mock (default) + llm-advisor
    (langchain.model-backed, same proposal-EDN contract)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate, :schedule-maintenance permanently absent from
    every phase's :auto set (structural, not a milestone)
  - Operation: MineralWoolOperationActor -- full langgraph-clj StateGraph
    (advise -> govern -> decide -> commit|hold|request-approval), real
    interrupt-before/resume approval workflow
  - Sim: demo runner (-main) exercising all four happy paths + ten HARD-hold
    scenarios directly
  - Ops (closed allowlist, all :effect :propose): log-production-batch
    (forming/curing batch, product-type/weight/thermal-conductivity/density
    data logging), schedule-maintenance (forming/curing-line-equipment
    maintenance scheduling), flag-safety-concern (fibre-exposure/equipment-
    safety -- ALWAYS escalates), coordinate-shipment (outbound shipment
    coordination)
  - Tests: 76 tests / 209 assertions across
    governor-contract/operation/phase/registry/store-contract, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-2399 (no rename
    needed)"

